   "status": "partial",
   "note": "has: Software Update checks pacman for the shell package and installs it after the person confirms, through the recovery guard (pacman_update.rs). Missing: security fixes for the rest of the system. The guard rejects base-system upgrades until a whole-root recovery path exists, and pacman output carries no advisory field, so a security-only install policy needs an advisory feed as well (for example arch-audit against the Arch security tracker, a lookup the person would have to consent to). Left open: it depends on the whole-root recovery design, which is not one agent's task.",
